Retry fstatvfs() on a plain descriptor when QNX refuses an O_DIRECTORY one.

QNX's fstatvfs() fails with ENOSYS on a descriptor opened with
O_DIRECTORY (checked on the targets: O_RDONLY works, O_RDONLY|O_DIRECTORY
does not), and smbd asks for a share's free space through the directory
handle it opened that way: every smbclient "ls" ended with "Error in
dskattr: NT_STATUS_NOT_SUPPORTED" (and exit status 1). On ENOSYS, retry on
a plain O_RDONLY descriptor of the same directory.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/lib/util/statvfs.c
+++ b/lib/util/statvfs.c
@@ -206,6 +206,20 @@
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = fstatvfs(fd, &statvfs_buf);
+#ifdef __QNX__
+	if (ret != 0 && errno == ENOSYS) {
+		/*
+		 * QNX: fstatvfs() of a descriptor opened with O_DIRECTORY
+		 * fails with ENOSYS; a plain O_RDONLY one of the same
+		 * directory works.
+		 */
+		int fd2 = openat(fd, ".", O_RDONLY);
+		if (fd2 != -1) {
+			ret = fstatvfs(fd2, &statvfs_buf);
+			close(fd2);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 
 	if (ret != 0) {
 		return ret;
